  "interpretation": "The normal facade's +0x27e6a8 caller loads x3 from the native header vector object at receiver+0x20, then +0x2830c4 saves that value at argument-array offset +0x20 before entering +0x168324.  The VM's direct x3 register is a separate image-relative constant, while its user argument remains in the packed array.  The independent output-reference continuation first loads x3 from [0x70002400+0x08] at +0x27e470 (observed on the following PC +0x27e474), yielding 0x101 before reaching the same +0x2830c4 wrapper.  Its x3 is therefore a different input role.  This explains why the -5 guard path cannot be selected by treating 0x101 as the facade header-vector pointer; it does not close signer semantics."
